  i.e. with the anchor as it actually stood), by phase:
    SH s42 r1: hold's last 2 s median 0.843 max 0.861 (n 1536-1562, 8 win) | after release median 0.843 max 0.894 (n 1525-1951, 153 win)
    SH s42 r2: hold's last 2 s median 0.844 max 0.859 (n 1536-1567, 8 win) | after release median 0.845 max 0.974 (n 1530-1877, 153 win)
    SH s7 r1: hold's last 2 s median 0.848 max 0.883 (n 1606-1696, 8 win) | after release median 0.841 max 0.893 (n 1611-1999, 153 win)
  The offline expired map (s43tau, G=0.9 τ=5) has no upward crossing; ask/n 0.87 at 1 024. With ask/n < 1 at every
  SH window, start-high descends; on the way down the anchor refreshes at the low point (brake ≈ 0 there, §42),
  so it settles where start-low does, unless the closed loop holds a crossing between 288 and 1 500 the ledgers
  do not sample (no oracle43 c2 window there outside transients).

